# fansboda-finance

Lightweight weekly pipeline: yfinance → SMA-50/200 + close → Neon Postgres. Runs on a GCP `e2-micro` VM via cron (Saturdays 11:00 UTC). ~$0/month target.

**Source of truth:** `.specify/memory/constitution.md` (principles) and the Spec Kit features in `specs/` (new requirements, design, migration steps). `project-docs/` (`PRD.md`, `FEATURES.md`, `MIGRATIONS.md`, `rfc/`) is the **frozen** baseline through RFC-018 / migration step 22 — read it for context, **never edit it**; put all new documentation in the feature's `specs/` folder.

## Scope (do not add without explicit request)

- No UI, API, auth layer, portfolio tracking, or extra indicators (EMA, RSI, MACD).
- No intraday/real-time data; weekly Saturday job only.
- `backfill_sma.py` is a **one-off manual** bootstrap — never cron-schedule it on production; run **per country set** (`--country us|swe|uk`, PRD FR-18).
- No alerting except the data-quality outlier email (PRD §5.9); Golden / Death Cross signals live in `fansboda`.
- Built: weekly growth columns ([RFC-016](project-docs/rfc/RFC-016-weekly-growth-columns.md), migration step 20) and the outlier guard + Gmail email ([RFC-017](project-docs/rfc/RFC-017-outlier-guard-email.md), no migration). Sector indices in `indices` replacing `*_by_sector` ([RFC-018](project-docs/rfc/RFC-018-sector-indices.md), migration steps 21–22). Out of scope until requested: corporate-actions table / correcting unadjusted series, dashboard, gap detection — see PRD §11.

